\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{8ca5a23}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The driver now accounts for time: per worker what was spent on a CPU, in the run queue, in collections and parked, the environment lane, a time series and a trace per unit. The account showed two things. The environment thread spent 4.0 of its 4.85 s on Mathlib adding up the shared bytes of the store after every step; it refreshes that sum at most every 20 ms now, and its CPU time fell from 4.69 s to 1.56 s. In later passes one batch of the whole file was cut into as many contiguous parts as there are workers, so that a heavy unit sat at the end of a part; a worker without work now takes the next slice of at most 256 units for itself.}

\p{Std with 8 workers, native image, quiet windows: check-only passes took 2.15 s before; with slices the median of 10 rounds is 1.67 s (-23 \%), the same as the bounded split that slices replaced (1.63 s). On Mathlib nothing changes beyond noise, as expected: the driver's waits are 1 \% there. Published with 106 tests, 103 green and 3 opt-in.}

\p{Detail: \src{docs/research/profiles/P7.md}, \src{rlvm-driver/README.md}. Commit \commit{8ca5a23}. Session: [profiles and prototypes](ses-JRSD). Related: [how the check phase scales](ins-MQ13), [the driver](design-driver).}
